    "notes": "The model reproduces the 420 m double-curvature arch, four recessed midlevel outlet mouths, four raised gate headworks, the separate power intake crane and the south thrust block. The signed placement fixes the 420 m arch at its 1145 m crest and the reservoir at 1140 m. The model trims mapped reservoir overlap along its upstream concrete face. The Earth fixture checks that native water no longer passes through the entire length of the sampled crest while preserving the downstream road, tunnel and building features. The retained PMTiles around the toe have a short river centerline and no continuous tailwater polygon. The terrain review fixture uses an illustrative downstream corridor. Outer reservoir banks remain angular in the coarse raster, which also obscures part of the south thrust block. The model shows static closed gates. Underground generation and operating discharge are outside the modeled exterior."
